      "player": "Opus Folksy",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Wait, Berg Strider blocked my Spark Reaper?! But Berg Strider had summoning sickness... again, summoning sickness doesn't prevent blocking. Darn.\n\
\n\
Berg Strider is 4/4 — it will kill my Spark Reaper (2/3), while my Reaper deals 2 damage to it, leaving it at 4/2. \n\
\n\
Hmm, I could activate Spark Reaper's ability ({3}, sacrifice a creature or planeswalker: gain 1 life and draw a card) to sacrifice it before combat damage. I'd lose Spark Reaper either way — I either sacrifice it and draw a card + gain 1 life, or it dies in combat for nothing. Sacrificing it is strictly better! I have 5 untapped lands (3 Swamps, 2 Forests), so I can pay the {3} cost.\n\
\n\
But wait — if I sacrifice it, it's removed from combat, so Berg Strider takes no combat damage. That means the 4/4 stays undamaged. Vs if combat happens, Berg Strider takes 2 damage and Spark Reaper dies. So it's: draw a card and gain 1 life, but opponent's Berg Strider stays at full health. vs. deal 2 damage to Berg Strider but lose Spark Reaper for nothing.\n\
\n\
Drawing a card is much more valuable than 2 damage on a creature I probably can't remove anyway. Let me sacrifice Spark Reaper to itself.",
