      "player": "Opus Folksy",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Turn 9. I'm at 1 life! This is extremely dire. I drew another Swamp. I have 8 untapped lands (3 Forests, 5 Swamps).\n\
\n\
Opponent has Berg Strider (4/4, tapped) and Goblin Shortcutter (2/1, tapped) from last attack, plus Avalanche Caller (1/3, untapped).\n\
\n\
Key: I MUST block everything this turn or I die. I need to think about what the opponent can attack with on their turn.\n\
\n\
My blockers: Roving Keep (5/7), Grave Bramble (3/4), Portcullis Vine (0/3). That's three blockers.\n\
\n\
Opponent's potential attackers: Berg Strider (4/4), Goblin Shortcutter (2/1), Avalanche Caller (1/3), plus any animated snow lands (4/4 hexproof). They have 3 Snow-Covered Islands and Avalanche Caller can animate them for {2} each. With 3 Mountains + 3 Snow Islands = 6 mana, they could animate potentially 3 snow lands (costs 6 mana) but each one also uses a land as the creature, reducing available mana.\n\
\n\
Wait, Goblin Shortcutter's ETB makes a creature unable to block. If they play another Shortcutter... but that's from hand, not from the battlefield one.\n\
\n\
The opponent could also use Icebind Pillar ({S}, {T}: tap target artifact or creature) to tap one of my blockers!\n\
\n\
My plan:\n\
1. Play Swamp (9 mana available)\n\
2. Cast Ossuary Rats ({5}{B} = 6 mana) — 3/2 that deals 1 damage ETB (1 creature in graveyard). Target Avalanche Caller (1/3) to kill it! This removes the snow land animation threat!\n\
3. That leaves 3 mana. I could also use Portcullis Vine's ability ({2}, {T}, sacrifice defender: draw a card) to sacrifice Portcullis Vine for a card draw if needed.\n\
\n\
Actually wait, killing Avalanche Caller is HUGE. Without it, they can't animate snow lands into 4/4 hexproof creatures. Their attack force becomes Berg Strider (4/4) + Goblin Shortcutter (2/1) = 6 damage. I can block with Roving Keep (5/7) on Berg Strider (kills it) and Grave Bramble (3/4) on Goblin Shortcutter (kills it). \n\
\n\
But they have Icebind Pillar to tap one of my blockers! If they tap Roving Keep, Berg Strider gets through for 4 and I die.\n\
\n\
Hmm. Let me cast Ossuary Rats first to kill Avalanche Caller, then think about blocking.\n\
\n\
Play Swamp, then Ossuary Rats.",
